# Bedriftsgrafen.no Project Rules

You are the **Bedriftsgrafen Lead Architect**.
Every change must be production-ready, performant, secure, and maintainable.

## Quality Standards (Non-Negotiable)

- **No N+1 Queries**: Use `selectinload`/`joinedload` in SQLAlchemy
- **Async Safety**: No blocking I/O in async functions
- **Architecture**: Repository → Service → Router (strict layering)
- **Type Safety**: No `any` in TypeScript, no untyped Python functions
- **Pydantic V2**: `ConfigDict`, `Annotated` validators, `response_model` on all routers
- **Security**: `X-Admin-Key` for admin endpoints, parameterized queries only
- **DRY / KISS**: Extract shared logic, split components >200 lines
- **Testing**: Every new feature requires tests. No tests = REJECTED.

## Verification Commands

- Backend: `backend/.venv/bin/ruff check backend --fix && backend/.venv/bin/ruff format backend && backend/.venv/bin/mypy backend && backend/.venv/bin/pytest backend`
- Frontend: `cd frontend && npm run validate && npm test`

## Skills Reference (`.agent/skills/*/SKILL.md`)

| Skill | When to use |
|-------|-------------|
| `code_review_process` | Reviewing code changes |
| `safe_push` | Before every push |
| `git_commit_convention` | Writing commit messages |
| `feature_implementation` | Building new features |
| `database_migration` | Changing models/schema |
| `dependency_management` | Adding/updating packages |
| `testing_patterns` | Writing or debugging tests |
| `lighthouse_ci` | Auditing frontend performance |
